# Nordshrift Synchro Component Model — NS-SYN-0001

Status: implementation model
Revision: 1.0.0
Date: September 2026

## Purpose

Defines the Synchro honest-measurement components exposed to Nordshrift/Sleela
builds. Synchro sends timestamped probes, matches replies, and reports the
MEASURED latency distribution. It makes no delivery-time guarantee.

## Metrics (closed)

sent, received, loss, mean, min, max, p95, report

## Invariants

- Honest by construction: measured, never promised. A lost probe is loss, never
  a fabricated latency.
- Bounded: a fixed probe table per VM; retained samples are bounded.
- Percentiles/mean report -1 when no sample has been received.

## Execution ABI

The core VM exposes Synchro as VM opcodes with VM-local probe handles:
`OP_SYN_OPEN`, `OP_SYN_DISPATCH`, `OP_SYN_STAT` (selector: sent/received/mean/
min/max/p95/loss), `OP_SYN_REPORT`, `OP_SYN_CLOSE`. These back the
`synchroOpen/synchroDispatch/synchro*/synchroReport/synchroClose` source
built-ins.

## SST guidance

See `SST.SYNCHRO.md` for the `measure:` block grammar and `examples/reach-measure.sst`.
